      "extract": "We now state some results on the zeros and critical points of random generalized polynomials. Let $(s_1, \\dots, s_k) \\in H^0(M, L^N)^k$ or let $(s_1, \\dots, s_k) \\in {\\mathcal H}_N^k$ in the real case. When $k = 1$ we omit the subscript. We will use the following notation. - $Z_s = \\{x : s(x) = 0\\}$ denotes the zero set of $s$, and $|Z_s|$ denotes the $m - k$-submanifold Riemannian volume density induced by $\\omega$",
